# Premade talent specs for aiplayerbot.conf (patch 0012)
#
# Hand-built level 60 specs against Turtle's reworked talent trees: one per role
# for every class, three each for druid, paladin, mage and warlock. The stock
# links that ship with the playerbot module are vanilla ones and every single
# one of them is rejected at startup.
#
# Each spec carries a levelling path in five level steps rather than only the
# level 60 link. ChangeTalentsAction::GetBestPremadeSpec hands out the first
# entry whose point total reaches the bot's, so with only a level 60 entry even
# a level 20 bot gets that one - and since talents are applied in tree order it
# would spend its first points in the secondary tree. A feral druid built to
# tank would start out as a balance caster.
#
# Replace the whole AiPlayerbot.PremadeSpec* block in aiplayerbot.conf with this.

